# Wall panel session — goes to ~/.config/labwc/autostart
#
# The Raspberry Pi session runs `labwc -m`, and --merge-config means every
# autostart file found is executed in turn, not just the first. So this file
# ADDS to /etc/xdg/labwc/autostart rather than replacing it: the desktop, the
# taskbar and kanshi are already started there and must not be repeated here,
# or they would run twice.
#
# The desktop and taskbar therefore keep running underneath. That is deliberate
# rather than merely tolerated: the browser covers them completely, and if it
# ever does exit, what appears is a working desktop instead of a black screen.
#
# To undo all of this: delete this file and reboot. Nothing else was changed,
# and nothing here needed root.

# No physical keyboard on a wall. Squeekboard stays hidden until a text field
# asks for it -- which is why Chromium is started with --enable-wayland-ime.
/usr/bin/squeekboard &

# The panel itself, brought back if it ever dies.
/usr/bin/lwrespawn "$HOME/panel-kiosk.sh" &
